-- [FilteringEnabled] Server Scripts are IMPOSSIBLE to save]]></ProtectedString><BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString><bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool><string name="Name"><![CDATA[AnimationLitePlayScript]]></string><BinaryString name="Tags"></BinaryString></Properties><Item class="TextBox" referent="549"><Properties><bool name="ClearTextOnFocus">false</bool><Font name="FontFace"><Family><url><![CDATA[rbxasset://fonts/families/Inconsolata.json]]></url></Family><Weight>400</Weight><Style>Normal</Style></Font><bool name="MultiLine">true</bool><bool name="RichText">true</bool><bool name="ShowNativeInput">false</bool><string name="Text"><![CDATA[----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--  AnimationLitePlayScript  --  This Script is automatically inserted into a Rig by  --
--  Studio Lite's "Animation Lite" if checkmarked while saving the KeyframeSequence.  --
--  You are free to change this script, place it inside Players, trigger it by GUI    --
--  or play it when a part is touched or a tool is equipped. Be sure to change the    --
--  script name so the checkmark in Animation Lite won't overwrite your work.         --
--                                                 --ScottSpiritWalker, 10/30/2025.   --
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

local AnimationLitePlayEvent = game.ServerScriptService.AnimationLiteService.AnimationLitePlayEvent
task.wait(1)  --wait for server to start so you can see the animation.
AnimationLitePlayEvent:Fire(script.Parent, script.KeyframeSequence.Value,1)   --Start playing animation and continue this script.  
--Parameters: rig, KeyframeSequence, speed=1, startKeyframe=1 and endKeyframe=9999
--The last two parameters can be used to pose a statue frozen at a particular frame number.


--------Request Stop playing an animation early, or stop a looped animation.
--while script.Parent:GetAttribute("AnimationLitePlaying") ~= nil do --stop currently playing animation if any.
--	script.Parent:SetAttribute("AnimationLitePlaying",false)
--	task.wait()
--end


--repeat	 --Wait for a non looped animation to end.
--	task.wait(.1)	
--until script.Parent:GetAttribute("AnimationLitePlaying") == nil

--The above examples are for NPC rigs. 


----------To fire this animation from a GUI button:
----------You will need a LocalScript in each Gui button (if more than one), something like these five lines:
